All 11 tests pass. The three static helpers on `CountingSort` are gone — `SortState` now fully owns its own construction.

**`SortState.from(int[] arr)`** is the static factory. It folds the three former helpers into a single pass: finds `min` and `max` together (one loop instead of two), validates the range, and builds the frequency array. It then constructs the `SortState` via the now-private constructor.

**`CountingSort.sort`** is reduced to its essential responsibility — input validation plus orchestration:

```java
SortState state = SortState.from(arr);
state.accumulateCounts();
return state.buildSorted();
```

`CountingSort` itself now has no private static helpers at all; all sorting logic lives in `SortState`.

